  "findings": {
    "mutable_inputs": "L1 fingerprinted a caller-owned draft list then stored its mutated value after the scope lock; derived output was validated before an await then published from caller-owned task/snapshot/prepared. Own all inputs before fingerprint/validation and first await; retained UoW is not copied; existing storage/security/CAS guards remain.",
    "unsupported_worker": "A worker without page-full-rebuild/1 could consume page dirty responsibility or supersede pending jobs. Filter owned definitions by capability before mutation and enforce the same contract at job creation.",
    "typed_idempotence": "Register enforces strict nonnegative integer generation; refresh force is an exact bool even on receipt replay, before idempotent return.",
    "output_budget": "Pure materialized_body is shared by full rebuild budget and guarded read; count the actual embedded block body representation with unchanged 32768-byte limit."
  },
  "review_scope": "Targeted code review of shared L1/derived transactional boundaries, current/history publication, graph authority, queue/readiness, capacity, erase and backup replay, plus final full regression of all previously enabled stages. Not an exhaustive proof of all code or planned features.",
